# THE MAPLIBRE NATIVE ANDROID SDK EVERY ANDROID BUILD SHIPS — named here and nowhere else (T978, owner 2026-11-22:
# "Pinned upstream main (Recommended)"). Sourced by build.sh, deploy/staging/build-apk.sh, deploy/lib/build-links.sh and
# app/tools/testbed/session.sh; read by tests. KEY=value lines only (no spaces, no expansion).
#
# WHY UPSTREAM MAIN, NOT A RELEASE TAG: the feature-state fix the app needs (T420; ours, upstream PR #4919, merged
# 2026-11-20 as 9cf8446d) is on main only. The newest Android release, android-v13.7.1 (2026-10-15), does not contain it,
# and the stock SDK re-applies every feature state to every tile every frame (T512: ~6 fps on the owner's Pixel). No patch
# of ours is applied: the old lean patch's second half (0002) measured within noise (T978, 2026-11-22) and is archived
# in archive-t420/.
#
# WHEN TO MOVE: to the first android-v* release tag that contains 9cf8446d (`git merge-base --is-ancestor 9cf8446d <tag>`).
# Then set MLN_COMMIT to that tag's commit and MLN_VERSION to its version with a local suffix, rebuild (build.sh), run the
# test bed's check (README.md), and say so in T978 — or drop the local build and take that version from Maven Central.
# Moving the pin to a newer main commit is the same steps.
MLN_COMMIT=3a6b955796b3509f184e9bf719e82cb2b432b958
# the local artifact's version (never a Maven Central one); names the commit, so a build id line says which source it is
MLN_VERSION=13.7.1-main.3a6b955
